---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Claude Community Cape Town collects through this website, why, and your rights under POPIA.">
  <PageHead title="Privacy notice" lede="What this site collects, why, and your rights under South Africa's Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA)." />
  <section class="wrap body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Claude Community Cape Town is a volunteer-run community, organised by the Claude Community Ambassadors named on the
        <a href="/">home page</a>. They are responsible for the personal information described here.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies and has no analytics or advertising trackers. If you switch between the light and dark
        theme, your choice is remembered in your own browser and is never sent to us. We only receive what you choose to type
        into one of two forms:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Give a talk:</strong> your name, email address and what you would like to talk about.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Host or support an event:</strong> your organisation, your name, your email address, a phone number and
          website if you give them, and your message.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The site is served by GitHub Pages, which keeps technical logs such as IP addresses for security. We do not have
        access to those logs.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        Only to reply to you about the talk or the offer you sent. We ask for it with your consent, which you give by
        sending the form. We do not use it for marketing, and we do not sell it or share it with anyone else.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is kept, and for how long</h2>
      <p>
        Form messages are stored in Google Forms, in a Google account only the volunteer hosts can open. Google may store
        this outside South Africa. We delete messages once they are no longer needed, and at the latest two years after
        you sent them.
      </p>

      <h2>Events</h2>
      <p>
        You register for events on Luma, which collects and holds your registration details under
        <a href="https://luma.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">its own privacy policy</a>. This site
        shows Luma's registration panel in a frame; anything you type there goes to Luma, not to us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="photos">Photos</h2>
      <p>
        We take photos at events and share some of them on this site. If you are in a photo and would like it taken down,
        message one of the hosts and we will remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask to see the personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, object to how we use
        it, or withdraw your consent at any time. To do any of these, message one of the hosts on LinkedIn (the links are
        under "Your hosts" on the <a href="/">home page</a>) and we will sort it out.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with how we handled your request, you may complain to the
        <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Information Regulator of South Africa</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this notice changes, the new version appears here. Its history is public in the
        <a href={SITE.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">site's repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .body {
    padding-bottom: var(--section);
  }
</style>
